BT 1 0 0 1 0 91 Tm /F2 10.5 Tf 14.5 TL 1.689622 Tw (Low-code development is an approach to building software applications mainly through visual tools and) Tj T* 0 Tw .142892 Tw (configuration instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.642109 Tw (visual development environments, predefined components and templates. Typical building blocks include) Tj T* 0 Tw .611039 Tw (forms for capturing data, reports and dashboards for viewing it, and workflows that define how information) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.251539 Tw (moves through a business process. In the Job Application Form application, for example, a form captures) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.801435 Tw (each job application, reports and a dashboard present the stored applications, and an approval workflow) Tj T* 0 Tw (moves each application through HR review.) Tj T* ET
